# starformation_and_feedback (S:995-1110) with R4's flags at substep 0 for the satellite of a real
# R4 FoF group at Snap_63, a hot-regime group whose forming satellite is in the CGM regime but holds
# only hot gas (real R4 evidence of the regime/reservoir disagreement): every routing follows the
# central (Regime 1), its CGM pair unselected; a stable disk after star formation.
# End-of-snapshot output values of the R4 reference output,
# /Volumes/Internal/results/sage26-campaign/workspace/e01-reference/out/R4/model_0.hdf5 (SHA-256
# 2b606ee7ac82559e32c7c91161f1edb44f89288ec57016e80da884e118ed0807), used as plausible call inputs,
# not reconstructed call-time state: the writer's verbatim floats, DiskScaleRadius the output's
# DiskRadius, MassLoading the stale value SAGE26 left (the FIRE path overwrites it), Regime the
# classifier's. Constructed: OutflowRate 0 (its value at substep 0 after the first-occupied reset,
# R/src/core_build_model.c:276) and zero histories, as at substep 0; the timing is the c05 R0
# templates' (c03's Age values). Each galaxy's stored SnapNum is the output snapshot and ZZ[SnapNum]
# SAGE26's 1/AA - 1.
# galaxy 0: R4 Snap_63 row 172 (GalaxyIndex 6000000000, Type 0, Regime 1)
# galaxy 1: R4 Snap_63 row 177 (GalaxyIndex 6000000125, Type 1, Regime 0)
# Reachability: R4-reachable.
# R4's flags (par/R4.par): CGMrecipeOn 1 (:54), FIREmodeOn 1 (:55), SFprescription 1 (:48),
# BulgeSizeOn 3 (:109), SupernovaRecipeOn 1 (:50), DiskInstabilityOn 1 (:52), AGNrecipeOn 2 (:49);
# every other parameter R3's (R4.par differs from R3.par only at :7 and :54).
format sage26-oracle-fixture 1
routine starformation_and_feedback_fire

